 xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:DisplayName>Name</b:DisplayName><b:Name/><b:Value i:type="c:string" xmlns:c="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">K8s Bridge -&gt; ARM Auto Hydration Flow&#xD;
====================&#xD;
Phase 1&#xD;
Resource Sync enqueues new write event&#xD;
Protocol: AMQP over TCP&#xD;
Identity: Azure Managed Identity&#xD;
Auth: Azure.Identity TokenCredential&#xD;
&#xD;
Phase 2&#xD;
Resource Sync/Hydration Engine processes new write event&#xD;
&#xD;
Phase 3&#xD;
Hydration Engine gets ARM Challenge Header&#xD;
Protocol: HTTPS (TLS 1.2+)&#xD;
Target: ARM Frontdoor&#xD;
&#xD;
Phase 4&#xD;
AAD Token Acquisition&#xD;
Identity: 1P App ID&#xD;
Creds: X.509 Certificate&#xD;
Library: MSAL (Microsoft.Identity.Client)&#xD;
Protocol: HTTPS to AAD STS&#xD;
&#xD;
Phase 5&#xD;
Resource Conversion + PUT to ARM Frontdoor&#xD;
Auth: Bearer token from phase 4 authenticates PUT to ARM&#xD;
Protocol: All traffic to ARM frontdoor is HTTPS&#xD;
