f the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>10. vmc binary is injected via iso 12. mTLS certs are injected via TLS encrypted RPC. 14. EnableArcAgent gRPC API is invoked with the required config as args including the rsa private key from step 7. 18. short lived TLS cert is rotated in exchange for a long lived leaf cert (1 year)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>7ca2df41-2d15-433b-afdc-476e1cb40eef</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R604a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba70acccaf2-2a61-4d48-9b95-4be00fd30d357ca2df41-2d15-433b-afdc-476e1cb40eef</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0acccaf2-2a61-4d48-9b95-4be00fd30d35</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>491</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7:0acccaf2-2a61-4d48-9b95-4be00fd30d35:7ca2df41-2d15-433b-afdc-476e1cb40eef</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by azlocal-vmc</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>azlocal-vmc claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>10. vmc binary is injected via iso 12. mTLS certs are injected via TLS encrypted RPC. 14. EnableArcAgent gRPC API is invoked with the required config as args including the rsa private key from step 7. 18. short lived TLS cert is rotated in exchange for a long lived leaf cert (1 year)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>7ca2df41-2d15-433b-afdc-476e1cb40eef</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T104a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba70acccaf2-2a61-4d48-9b95-4be00fd30d357ca2df41-2d15-433b-afdc-476e1cb40eef</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0acccaf2-2a61-4d48-9b95-4be00fd30d35</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>490</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7:0acccaf2-2a61-4d48-9b95-4be00fd30d35:7ca2df41-2d15-433b-afdc-476e1cb40eef</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Lack of Input Validation for azlocal-vmc</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across 10. vmc binary is injected via iso 12. mTLS certs are injected via TLS encrypted RPC. 14. EnableArcAgent gRPC API is invoked with the required config as args including the rsa private key from step 7. 18. short lived TLS cert is rotated in exchange for a long lived leaf cert (1 year) may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against azlocal-vmc or an elevation of privilege attack against azlocal-vmc or an information disclosure by azlocal-vmc. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>10. vmc binary is injected via iso 12. mTLS certs are injected via TLS encrypted RPC. 14. EnableArcAgent gRPC API is invoked with the required config as args including the rsa private key from step 7. 18. short lived TLS cert is rotated in exchange for a long lived leaf cert (1 year)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>7ca2df41-2d15-433b-afdc-476e1cb40eef</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5486601d8-829e-4939-9159-bca98b8bdc3bdd014b58-03a1-4a0d-b09b-404b632d2012ec5d9426-a2d3-47d9-be0e-6bd53b655e2c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f2963659-3f3c-4bde-aadb-d2b6df386b61</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>dd014b58-03a1-4a0d-b09b-404b632d2012</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>156</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>486601d8-829e-4939-9159-bca98b8bdc3b:dd014b58-03a1-4a0d-b09b-404b632d2012:ec5d9426-a2d3-47d9-be0e-6bd53b655e2c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Azure Key Vault may be able to impersonate the context of Azure Key Vault A4S ext in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>HTTPS (OauthMI)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>486601d8-829e-4939-9159-bca98b8bdc3b</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>ec5d9426-a2d3-47d9-be0e-6bd53b655e2c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D4486601d8-829e-4939-9159-bca98b8bdc3bdd014b58-03a1-4a0d-b09b-404b632d2012ec5d9426-a2d3-47d9-be0e-6bd53b655e2c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f2963659-3f3c-4bde-aadb-d2b6df386b61</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>dd014b58-03a1-4a0d-b09b-404b632d2012</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>155</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>486601d8-829e-4939-9159-bca98b8bdc3b:dd014b58-03a1-4a0d-b09b-404b632d2012:ec5d9426-a2d3-47d9-be0e-6bd53b655e2c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow HTTPS (OauthMI) Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a