tringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>9. A chain of requests from the overlay extension to vmo manipulate the Windows HyperV fabric through HyperV and Windows APIs to achieve the intent of the VM CR. This request includes a TLS cert bundle with a short lived leaf cert.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>57e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E557e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace30af73cb-b8e7-4437-9ff2-13f16a6bdfad04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>30af73cb-b8e7-4437-9ff2-13f16a6bdfad</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>292</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>57e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace:30af73cb-b8e7-4437-9ff2-13f16a6bdfad:04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>azlocal-vmo may be able to impersonate the context of azlocal-overlay extension in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>9. A chain of requests from the overlay extension to vmo manipulate the Windows HyperV fabric through HyperV and Windows APIs to achieve the intent of the VM CR. This request includes a TLS cert bundle with a short lived leaf cert.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>57e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E657e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace30af73cb-b8e7-4437-9ff2-13f16a6bdfad04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>30af73cb-b8e7-4437-9ff2-13f16a6bdfad</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>293</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>57e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace:30af73cb-b8e7-4437-9ff2-13f16a6bdfad:04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>azlocal-vmo May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>azlocal-overlay extension may be able to remotely execute code for azlocal-vmo.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>9. A chain of requests from the overlay extension to vmo manipulate the Windows HyperV fabric through HyperV and Windows APIs to achieve the intent of the VM CR. This request includes a TLS cert bundle with a short lived leaf cert.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>57e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E757e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace30af73cb-b8e7-4437-9ff2-13f16a6bdfad04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>30af73cb-b8e7-4437-9ff2-13f16a6bdfad</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>294</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>57e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace:30af73cb-b8e7-4437-9ff2-13f16a6bdfad:04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in azlocal-vmo</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into azlocal-vmo in order to change the flow of program execution within azlocal-vmo to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>9. A chain of requests from the overlay extension to vmo manipulate the Windows HyperV fabric through HyperV and Windows APIs to achieve the intent of the VM CR. This request includes a TLS cert bundle with a short lived leaf cert.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>57e39ef3-c10b-4386-aa0f-146cb4645ace</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>04a79eec-77ec-4a54-8692-7a2c1a862ba7</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S1137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f82402837398-3550-4e8e-b068-763a4d6d114316ca605e-1063-4ad2-8508-ef47cfc21440</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>02837398-3550-4e8e-b068-763a4d6d1143</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>295</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824:02837398-3550-4e8e-b068-763a4d6d1143:16ca605e-1063-4ad2-8508-ef47cfc21440</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the azcmagent Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>azcmagent may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Hybrid Identity. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From azcmagent to Hybrid Identity via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>16ca605e-1063-4ad2-8508-ef47cfc21440</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R6137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f82402837398-3550-4e8e-b068-763a4d6d114316ca605e-1063-4ad2-8508-ef47cfc21440</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>02837398-3550-4e8e-b068-763a4d6d1143</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>296</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824:02837398-3550-4e8e-b068-763a4d6d1143:16ca605e-1063-4ad2-8508-ef47cfc21440</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by Hybrid Identity</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Hybrid Identity claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From azcmagent to Hybrid Identity via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>16ca605e-1063-4ad2-8508-ef47cfc21440</b:TargetGuid><b:Ti