g advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>azcmagent may be able to impersonate the context of azlocal-vmc in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>15. vmc downloads a hybrid compute managed script and runs it. The script installs azcmagent. vmc runs "azcmagent connect existing" with args and connects the VM to the hybrid compute machine created in step 2.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>7ca2df41-2d15-433b-afdc-476e1cb40eef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S1137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824e6633d5c-5e08-44b9-a7d4-6173896f0ee96bf3a0a5-1257-4556-bca4-146fba7b0ac7</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e6633d5c-5e08-44b9-a7d4-6173896f0ee9</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>303</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824:e6633d5c-5e08-44b9-a7d4-6173896f0ee9:6bf3a0a5-1257-4556-bca4-146fba7b0ac7</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the azcmagent Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>azcmagent may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to ARC RP. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From azcmagent to ARC RP via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>6bf3a0a5-1257-4556-bca4-146fba7b0ac7</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R6137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824e6633d5c-5e08-44b9-a7d4-6173896f0ee96bf3a0a5-1257-4556-bca4-146fba7b0ac7</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e6633d5c-5e08-44b9-a7d4-6173896f0ee9</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>304</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824:e6633d5c-5e08-44b9-a7d4-6173896f0ee9:6bf3a0a5-1257-4556-bca4-146fba7b0ac7</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by ARC RP</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>ARC RP claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From azcmagent to ARC RP via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>6bf3a0a5-1257-4556-bca4-146fba7b0ac7</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D3137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824e6633d5c-5e08-44b9-a7d4-6173896f0ee96bf3a0a5-1257-4556-bca4-146fba7b0ac7</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e6633d5c-5e08-44b9-a7d4-6173896f0ee9</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>305</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-