b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S7.1e899895e-9794-4a38-b6d9-d0e0cd12398a04d91933-1141-4d2d-bb69-c1005a0e04207ce257bb-c26f-4a2e-9d48-2a09042cc001</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>04d91933-1141-4d2d-bb69-c1005a0e0420</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>310</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e899895e-9794-4a38-b6d9-d0e0cd12398a:04d91933-1141-4d2d-bb69-c1005a0e0420:7ce257bb-c26f-4a2e-9d48-2a09042cc001</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of Destination Data Store Windows Local Machine Cert Store</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Windows Local Machine Cert Store may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of Windows Local Machine Cert Store. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Stores mTLS certs</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e899895e-9794-4a38-b6d9-d0e0cd12398a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>7ce257bb-c26f-4a2e-9d48-2a09042cc001</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S7.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D2e899895e-9794-4a38-b6d9-d0e0cd12398a04d91933-1141-4d2d-bb69-c1005a0e04207ce257bb-c26f-4a2e-9d48-2a09042cc001</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>04d91933-1141-4d2d-bb69-c1005a0e0420</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>311</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e899895e-9794-4a38-b6d9-d0e0cd12398a:04d91933-1141-4d2d-bb69-c1005a0e0420:7ce257bb-c26f-4a2e-9d48-2a09042cc001</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for Azure Key Vault A4S ext or Windows Local Machine Cert Store</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Does Azure Key Vault A4S ext or Windows Local Machine Cert Store take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Stores mTLS certs</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e899895e-9794-4a38-b6d9-d0e0cd12398a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>7ce257bb-c26f-4a2e-9d48-2a09042cc001</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S1137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f8244e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a1692da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>312</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824:4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169:2da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the azcmagent Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>azcmagent may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Hybrid Compute. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From azcmagent to Hybrid Compute via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>2da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R6137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f8244e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a1692da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>313</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824:4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169:2da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by Hybrid Compute</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Hybrid Compute claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From azcmagent to Hybrid Compute via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>2da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D3137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f8244e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a1692da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>314</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824:4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169:2da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Process Crash or Stop for Hybrid Compute</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Hybrid Compute crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From azcmagent to Hybrid Compute via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>2da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D4137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f8244e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a1692da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>315</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824:4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169:2da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow  Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From azcmagent to Hybrid Compute via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>2da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f8244e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a1692da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>8c022810-2a7f-459b-98ff-72b811a8ed65</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>316</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>137b7f37-2b24-4cb1-853f-d47e5a27f824:4e7ad9b7-c283-4868-8db8-71eff5f9a169:2da3e4df-1bb0-4c43-b9e3-f635100f5050</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil=